      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-10-07_WidnesExaminer_art0083" n="art0083">
        <head>NY DEAR CHILDREN,</head>
        <p>NY DEAR CHILDREN,</p>
        <p>Very many thanks for several etoryettes received during the last few days. I shall pula lish one or two of the best next week. I can quite underetand that some of you are rather nfmid to semi me anything, in case it should not be quite up to the mark. Now this is a great pity, ae I am very pleased to receive any communications.</p>
        <p>Further down these columns you will find a set of punles ; to the sender of the first correct solution I Will give a beautiful box of Fry's chocolate.</p>
        <p>I hope I shall be receiving a good number of new niembns during.the next- week. You will remember that a week or two since I mentioned that I was anxious that our list; of new members should he increased to a thousand. Any of you wishing to receive sheets on which to enter namos can have same on writing to me. We want to make our League as strong as poseible, and to increase it every week. Remember the motto printed in our columns a few weeks since. Do your utmost among your little friends. A little later on I shall give full particulars of our Competitions for Christmas. I shall get some beautiful boxes of Fry's chocolate as prizes. ThEsc, I am sure, will be much appre- .</p>
        <p>Ciated. as they will make very nice presents at that 'season of the year.</p>
        <p>With love from</p>
        <p>UNTCLE NED.</p>
