        <p>BATHING IN THE SHIP CANAL. At Tuesday night's meeting of the Sale Council an important letter was read from the Ship Canal Com- pany with reference to a letter from the Council calling attention to the danger arising from persons bathing in the canal at Sale, and asking the company to take measures to prevent it as far as possible. The letter points out that the company are desirous of preventing bathing in the canal, tad have for some time posted notices in prominent places prohibiting the practice, but it is very difficult to stop it. The gallant conduct of Mr. J. A. Gee, of Sale, in rescuing a lad from drowning in the Strid. near Bolton Abbey, has been recognized by the presentation to him of the Royal Humane Society's certificate.</p>
